`coe_sSup_of_directed` says the underlying sequence of a nonempty directed supremum is the pointwise supremum. The identities \(x = \bigsqcup_n i_{n\infty}(x_n)\) and the supremum of the approximating projections are [directed suprema](1972_Directed_suprema.md). Scott states those identities and not this computation. **Theorem:** yes — the pointwise formula is formalized. **Proof:** yes — compatibility of the pointwise supremum, the upper-bound comparison, and uniqueness of the least upper bound.
